{#incident}
@summary: Incident response timeline template
# Incident Timeline

- T+00m: Detect alert and declare incident.
- T+05m: Assign incident commander and scribe.
- T+15m: Publish first customer update.
- T+30m: Choose mitigation or rollback path via {@rollback}.

After stabilization, complete {@postmortem}.
{/incident}

{#rollback}
@summary: Rollback steps with commands
# Rollback Steps

1. Pause deploys.
2. Roll back to last known good release.
3. Validate health checks and traffic recovery.

```
./deploy freeze
./deploy rollback --service api --to release-2026-02-01
./deploy status --service api
```

If recovery succeeds, document outcomes in {@postmortem}.
{/rollback}

{#postmortem}
@summary: Post-incident writeup outline
# Postmortem Outline

Summary:
Capture impact window, severity, and affected customers.

Root Cause:
List direct cause and contributing factors.

Action Items:
- [ ] Fix root cause permanently.
- [ ] Add guardrail monitoring.
- [ ] Update this runbook with learnings.
{/postmortem}
